{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Mount Hor.</b> You go around and walk to the northern pass on the eastern side, and you reach the entrance of Hamat — this is Antiochia." "<b>The outgoings of the border.</b> The ends of the border. Everywhere that תּוֹצְאוֹת הַגְּבוּל is stated — either the border ends there completely and does not pass beyond at all, or from there it spreads and widens and extends behind to continue onward diagonally more than the first width. And with respect to the first measured width it called them תּוֹצָאוֹת, for there that measure ended."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:44.679343771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}